          "source_text_sha256": "7466e1ee34c3c80761dd6f25513e6175b4682f8f3e4f9c98d3809f64a2655f2e",
          "start_ms": null,
          "status": "needs-review",
          "text": "Description: On December 26th and 29th, 2014, gendarmes were contacted by two witnesses residing in a hamlet within the commune of Nizerolles (03) who were intrigued by the presence of various lights in the night sky (see the investigation report). Based on the evidence collected, including: - The existence of regulated nighttime lighting tests on wind turbines located approximately 12 kilometers from the witnesses, partially visible in the observation axis, confirmed by on-site gendarmes. These lights are the same red color as two of the observed lights. - The presence of the planet Jupiter, observed in the same axis, moving and of the same color as one of the lights. - Public lighting of a nearby hamlet, witness #1 confusion noted by the gendarmes. - Christmas light decorations, witness #1 confusion also noted by the gendarmes. - The existence, for one witness, of a physiological phenomenon of micro-ocular mobility (\"micro-nystagmus\"). We can conclude that the lights observed by the witnesses are very likely a combination of various natural or man-made phenomena and objects (Jupiter, wind turbine red lights, public lighting, Christmas lights...) accompanied, for most, by the micro-nystagmus phenomenon. This case is classified as \"A\" for a certain observation of nighttime lighting of wind turbines, the planet Jupiter, and public lighting.",
          "translation_text_sha256": "e2ce2d7833a7521d5ece16afe95f51f1c7390a74559a458f4b51d106a66d6959"
        }
      ],
